course: dictionary
lesson: 2138
title: Working together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: If you are cooperative, you are willing to help others and do what is asked. «Ollie's family plays cooperative games, where everyone works together against the game.» Here cooperative describes the games: the players are on the same team, working towards one goal.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Working together, and winning or losing together, both point to one meaning: helping each other. Test it by swapping in "helping each other" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The same word can also name a thing. A cooperative is a business or farm owned and run by the people who work in it or use it, and they share the profits. A «co-op» is a short way of saying cooperative, like the Co-op shop, which is owned by its members.
fact: Cooperative means willing to help and work together with others.
fact: A cooperative game is one where everyone wins or loses together.
fact: An uncooperative person is stubborn and will not help, so it is the opposite of cooperative.
fact: A cooperative is a business or farm owned and run by the people who work in it or use it.
fact: The members of a cooperative share its profits.
exercise: «Ollie's family plays cooperative games, where everyone works together against the game.» What does cooperative mean here? | Expensive to buy | Very noisy and fast | *Working together towards the same goal | Playing alone and keeping score
exercise: In a cooperative game, what happens to the players? | *Everyone wins or loses together | They take turns to sulk | One player always loses | Only the best player wins
exercise: Which word means the opposite of cooperative, for someone who will not help? | Patient | Helpful | *Uncooperative | Generous
test: Ruby says, «The Co-op is a shop owned by its members.» What is a co-op? | *A shop owned by its members | A school for swimming lessons | A castle on a hill | A game played with cards
test: In cooperative learning, what do students do? | Compete for the top mark | *Work in groups and help each other | Work alone in silence | Sit in rows and never talk
exam: Mia says, «Our cooperative shares its profits between the people who work in it.» What does cooperative mean here? | A very old castle | A quiet, sulky child | *A business owned and run by the people who work in it | A game where players take turns to sulk
